*Adjectives* are words that describe or modify nouns. In the sentences _an old book_ and _the book is old_, _old_ is an adjective. 
Note how you can put the adjective before the noun (_an old book_) or link the noun and adjective with _to be_ (_the book is old_)? It works the same in Dutch: _een oud boek_ (_an old book_) and _het boek is oud_ (_the book is old_). 

In this skill, you will learn some adjectives and use them to describe nouns using _zijn_ (_to be_).